    "body": "## Summary\n\nADR-039 Commit 1: `height` application + `min/max` clamps + `overflow: hidden` clipping. **Closes ADR-037's deferred height gap** (search icon w=20 h=0 → w=20 h=20). **Introduces an honest, measured ~185px gap** between header and article title — cause not yet diagnosed, hypothesis and deferral documented.\n\n## The verified fix: ADR-037's height gap closed\n\n| Check | Post-ADR-037 | Post-ADR-039 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search icon width | 20 | 20 |\n| Search icon height | **0** | **20** |\n\n`height` is now applied to all boxes, not just `<img>`. The search icon (has `height: calc(1rem + 4px)` in Wikipedia CSS) now correctly renders at 20×20.\n\n## The honest finding: ~185px gap\n\n| Element | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Article title \"HTML\" | y≈145 | **y≈330** |\n| Total layout height | 62295 | 62283 (−12) |\n\n**185px of content moved from the article body to the gap above it.** Total height essentially unchanged.\n\n**Cause: NOT YET MEASURED.** Hypothesis: `min-height` values on header-chrome elements (`.mw-page-container`, `.mw-header`, `.vector-page-titlebar`, `.vector-page-toolbar`) that were previously ignored now stack to ~185px. Wikipedia's CSS specifies real minimums that our layout was compressing.\n\n- **If hypothesis is correct**: this is expected chrome spacing (the header is genuinely supposed to be taller).\n- **If not**: this is a real bug (some element incorrectly getting a min-height).\n\n**Deferred to a quick post-merge diagnostic.** Search-icon fix is verified and real; the gap needs measurement before we claim it as expected.\n\n## What shipped\n\n### 1. Height applied to all boxes (percentage-skipped)\n\nPercentage heights are **skipped in v1** — `LengthContext` has no `parent_content_height`, so `height: 100%` on `<html>`/`<body>` would resolve against viewport *width* (1774px) and collapse the whole layout. This was discovered during implementation (initial version without the skip collapsed layout height to 1774px). **Reverted and fixed before commit.**\n\nThreading `parent_content_height` is ADR-040.\n\n### 2. min/max-width clamps\n\nAfter width resolution. `vw`/`vh` in value skips the clamp (ADR-037 defers those units; would collapse the element to 0px otherwise). Percentages work fine — `parse_length` already uses `parent_content_width`.\n\n### 3. min/max-height clamps\n\nSame `vw`/`vh`/percentage skip rules.\n\n### 4. `overflow: hidden` paint clipping\n\nSets `LayoutBox::clip_children`. `paint.cpp` wraps children paint in `cairo_save` + clip rectangle + `cairo_restore`. `hidden auto` also sets it (v1 treats two-value as hidden on both axes). `auto`/`scroll` unchanged.\n\n### 5. Dup cleanup (bonus)\n\nRemoved the duplicated ADR-035 img sizing block (identical text appeared twice; second occurrence was dead code from an earlier mis-applied patch).\n\n## What's still deferred\n\n- `height: %` / `min-height: %` / `max-height: %` — `parent_content_height` threading (ADR-040)\n- `max-width: min(..., vw)` — same vw unit deferral\n- `overflow: auto | scroll` — scrollbar + event subsystem, own ADR\n- `overflow-wrap` — typography, not box model\n- `aspect-ratio` — 0 uses in target CSS\n- `box-sizing: border-box` — **Commit 2** (isolated risk)\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before: 480 / 1851\n- After: **494 / 1881** (+14 / +30)\n- Full suite all pass, zero warnings\n\nNew `tests/test_box_model.cpp` (14 tests):\n- Height applied, taller content capped, auto no-op, **percentage skipped**\n- min-width / max-width raise/cap, none no-op, vw-in-max-width skipped\n- min-height / max-height, none no-op\n- overflow: hidden sets flag, visible/auto don't, hidden auto does\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Search icon h=0 → h=20 | ✅ |\n| Article title y=145 → 330 | ⚠️ (cause unmeasured, hypothesis documented) |\n| Total layout height ~62283 | ✅ (62295 baseline, −12) |\n| 14 box-model tests pass | ✅ |\n| Full suite 494 / 1881 | ✅ |\n| No collapse to 1774px | ✅ (percentage skip applied) |\n\n## What's next\n\n1. **Post-merge**: quick diagnostic to confirm/refute the min-height-stack hypothesis (or identify actual cause)\n2. **Commit 2**: `box-sizing: border-box` — isolated for revertability\n3. **ADR-040**: `parent_content_height` threading (unblocks percentage heights), `overflow: auto/scroll`, `aspect-ratio`\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Percentage skip accepted** — required to prevent collapse; ADR-040 threading is correct home for unblocking\n- [ ] **185px gap documented as UNMEASURED** — hypothesis is min-height stack, deferred to post-merge diagnostic; not claimed as expected behavior\n- [ ] **`overflow: hidden auto` treated as `hidden`** — v1 limitation\n- [ ] **Dup cleanup accepted** — bonus in the same commit, removes dead code\n\nRefs #198\n",
